  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes a hybrid quantum–classical graph neural network (QGNN) using 7‑qubit parameterized circuits (90 trainable parameters) as message‑passing layers. On the Cora dataset the best QGNN reaches 59.6% accuracy versus 79.0% for a classical GCN, while on a NIFTY50 stock‑movement task the QGNN achieves F1 scores around 0.58–0.59, roughly comparable to classical baselines. All experiments are performed on the PennyLane default.qubit noiseless simulator.",
